{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities","id":1154067,"title":"My Alternate Solar Favored Abilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-30T00:17:26-07:00","id":1154067,"title":"My Alternate Solar Favored Abilities","content":"This isn't a functional rule set. Its just a personal view of how I personally felt Exalted could be in the mechanics of its design. I love the world of Exalted, the Lore, the ideas - but the game rules are too convoluted for me and my group. So we're basically sticking to DnD and the like.<br /> <br /> That said, I am a stubborn person, and I need to vent my creativity in unusual ways :P So I came up with a version of how I feel the Solars should favor their abilities, which:<br /> - merged some of the pre-existing abilities for mechanical streamlining<br /> - shared favored abilities around more (aka no more &quot;you can only choose Archery as your Supernal ability if you are Dawn Caste&quot;)<br /> - still kept certain abilities in each Solar Group being Supernal abilities<br /> <br /> So, before getting into it, I want to cover what abilities got Merged:<br /> - Dodge and Athletics got merged into &quot;Acrobatics&quot; (though the more 'strength based' athletics got merged into a different ability; see next)<br /> - Athletics and Resistance got merged into &quot;Vigor&quot; (basically streamlining mobility effects VS power effects)<br /> - Investigation got merged into &quot;Perception&quot; (both are based on observational skills; though some Investigation rolls would probably use Lore)<br /> - Presence got merged into single &quot;Presence&quot; (Performance is basically a variation of 'look at me' - so it made sense that both abilities designed to draw a crowd should be a single trait)<br /> - Ride and Survival got merged into &quot;Wildlife&quot; (with exception of only a few charms; the majority of Survival Charms was about dealing with a familiar. And survival rolls can be suplemented for a Lore roll for how well you KNOW how to SURVIVE or something similar).<br /> <br /> With that covered, let's get into my Caste/ Ability assignment:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Dawn</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Brawl</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Melee</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Archery</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Thrown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">War</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Vigor</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Zenith</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Occult</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Presence</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lore</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">War</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wildlife</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Vigor</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Twilight</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Craft</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Medicine</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lore</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Perception</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sail</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Acrobatics</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Night</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Larceny</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Stealth</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Archery</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Thrown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Perception</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Acrobatics</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Eclipse</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Bureaucracy</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Socialize</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sail</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wildlife</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Acrobatics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Vigor</td> </tr> </table></div> This spread gives each Caste two exclusively favored Abilities (see the first two emboldened columns), and gives each Caste at least either Vigor or Acrobatics for a defensive ability (Vigor for toughening out damage, Acrobatics for avoiding it).<br /> <br /> There is also an ability bridge into each Caste - Dawn and Zenith both have War, Zenith and Twilight both have Lore, Twilight and Night both have Perception, and Night and Dawn have Archery AND Thrown. This is slightly for flavor, giving the feel that each Caste Flows into the next (Eclipse is the exception, though they share Sail with Twilight, and Wildlife with the Zenith).<br /> <br /> This also means, with exception of two exclusive Abilities per cast, EVERY other ability is favored by two Castes (.<br /> <br /> This DOES change the roles of each Caste member of course (e.g.: why does Zenith have Occult instead of Twilight?), but I've looked into that as well:<ul><li>Dawn are the Warriors who charge the Darkness and make it Run (pretty standard)</li> <li>Zenith are the Leaders who bask in the Light and are noticed - through either drawing and addressing Crowds or Armies, Educating the Masses to make them 'Enlightened', or casting Epic Sorceries that reshape the landscape. Everything about a Zenith is about being seen and noticed (the opposite of a Night caste - see below)</li> <li>Twilight are the Problem Solvers, who reflect on a newly approaching problem (i.e.: the darkness) and find a solution. They build devices and sail on their creations, and find new ways to heal new afflictions.</li> <li>Night are the Assassins and Spies. They fight with misdirection and through espionage. They are the secondary Warriors (to the Dawn) who attack from a distance with Arrows and Throwing blades; killing without being seen.</li> <li>Eclipse are the Deal Makers. They travel on Horseback or Ship to their meetings, overcoming any obstruction through strength or agility, to bartner agreements through seductive interaction or logistical bureaucracy. Their role is to not to be seen or heard (like a Zenith) but rather negotiate and find social solutions.</li> </ul>For me, I feel this works, though a lot of the rebalancing would come from the Caste Abilities (which I think do deserve some attention and not just be &quot;tacked on&quot; abilities).<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ________________________<br /> <br /> Regardless it an unofficial idea which is probably not going to be considered. But its an idea I've had. And I figured instead of letting it rot in my brain, I'd share it on the grounds maybe someone gets inpsired by it for their own work.<br /> <br /> Enjoy, discuss, or discard at your leisure! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T09:02:56-07:00","id":1154134,"title":"","content":"A few things.<br /> <br /> First, if you reduce Abilities (and presuming that Charms are merged?) and don't adjust the character creation process, then PCs will be 'better' than otherwise, as at the least they are less spread out.<br /> <br /> Second, if you combine Presence and Performance, I would suggest combining Bureaucracy and Socialize. P&amp;P are the 'in your face' social influence Abilities, while BS (heh) are the 'behind the scenes' social influence Abilities.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I would try to get the Abilities down to 15 so that no Caste has a monopoly on any Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:26:02-07:00","id":1154158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154134#post1154134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I would try to get the Abilities down to 15 so that no Caste has a monopoly on any Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanna break Dawns? Because that's how you break Dawns. A monopoly on supernal combat abilities is the heavy lifter in their &quot;actually best at combat this edition&quot; thing. <br /> <br /> Also <i>Zenith</i> being the only ones to get occult? Zenith. Seriously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T21:49:56-07:00","id":1154293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities#post1154067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the game rules are too convoluted for me and my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you could just tell us which bits are giving you difficulty, and we can help you.<br /> <br /> Also, I second Elfive's &quot;WTF only Zeniths get Occult?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T02:43:21-07:00","id":1154317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154134#post1154134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things.<br /> <br /> First, if you reduce Abilities (and presuming that Charms are merged?) and don't adjust the character creation process, then PCs will be 'better' than otherwise, as at the least they are less spread out.<br /> <br /> Second, if you combine Presence and Performance, I would suggest combining Bureaucracy and Socialize. P&amp;P are the 'in your face' social influence Abilities, while BS (heh) are the 'behind the scenes' social influence Abilities.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I would try to get the Abilities down to 15 so that no Caste has a monopoly on any Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice feedback! Ty.<br /> <br /> 1) I agree character creation will need be adjusted with this. My idea is to go with characters choosing a Primary Supernal Ability, AND a Secondary Supernal Ability. The Primary must be from their Favored Ability (as listed), and they treat the purchasing of Charms for that Ability as if their Essence was +2 Higher (aka they can have up to Essence 3 Charms in that ability).<br /> <br /> The Secondary Ability can be ANY ability (not just the favored) and they treat charm purchase as if their Essence was +1 Higher (so they can have Essence 2 Charms for that Ability). It spreads the character creation options around for more interesting combos, while still encouraging theme of what your character is &quot;destined&quot; to be good at.<br /> <br /> 2) I also like the merging of the BS <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was toying with it for a while myself, creating the &quot;Bargen&quot; ability (the term gives enough leeway to be making deals - socially or fomally), and think I will go with it. It DOES cause the Eclipse to have only 4 Favored Abilities (instead of everyone else having 5) but I may tweak their Caste Abilities to compensate - sorta like how they already have the ability to learn non-Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> 3) The way its going, its probably going to drop to 16. Can't quite break it to the 15th level, but I think its pretty solid where it is now. The reviewed Chart (mering &quot;Bureacracy and Socialize&quot;, &quot;Brawl with Melee&quot; [you can specialize in Unarmed or a Weapon for either effect], and discarding Sail - its Charms will probably find its place in Craft, War, Occult and Presence depending on their function) now looks like this:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dawn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Melee</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Archery</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Thrown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">War</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Vigor</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Zenith</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Occult</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Presence</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lore</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">War</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Vigor</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Twilight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Craft</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Medicine</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lore</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Perception</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Acrobatics</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Night</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Larceny</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Stealth</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Perception</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Thrown</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Acrobatic</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Eclipse</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Bargen</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Wildlife</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">n/a</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Acrobatics</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Vigor</i></td> </tr> </table></div> 16 Abilities in Total, 10 Exclusive to their Caste, 6 shared between at least 2 Castes. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154158#post1154158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wanna break Dawns? Because that's how you break Dawns. A monopoly on supernal combat abilities is the heavy lifter in their &quot;actually best at combat this edition&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Also <i>Zenith</i> being the only ones to get occult? Zenith. Seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dawn are still the Combat Engines they were designed to be. They retain exclusivity for Supernal Melee and Archery, sharing Thrown with the Night Assassins and War with the Leadership of the Zenith. If needed their Caste Abilities will be improved for more Combative Power, so they are still the Brutes and Champions they are destined to be - though I'd like them to have an innate ability to be Intimidating (which they kinda do have) so they have some involvement OFF the battlefield.<br /> <br /> As for the Zenith getting Occult, I think its fine. And your statement of &quot;seriously&quot; doesn't give me any grounds to reply to your objection. So to respond to you and Hakkonen, my thinking behind it was that the Zenith are &quot;BIG&quot;. They are designed to be SEEN. Like the Sun at its peak, people notice them. So their actions are BIG. Nation shaking. They rally crowds into riots, or organize them into Armies. They manipulate energy that reshapes landscapes, devistates nations, changes the history books, etc... They are BIG. Their actions are ground shaking. It ties into their connection to their God - and as living champions of the sun, they use this power to bring change. Sometimes even directed by the UCS itself.<br /> <br /> As for why the Twilight and Eclipse loose this, its because thematically these two work in a different direction. The Twilight are still big, but their epic creations are physical. They create weapons, warstriders, fortresses, temples, Manses, armors, tools. Their magic exists in the Forge and the Pen. Their structure is more defensive, which comes from the theme of the Light Fading, and them fortifying their homes to survive the darkness until the Light comes. Sorcery is almost typically offensive, so it worked against the Twilight Theme.<br /> <br /> And the Eclipse are Deal Makers and Negotiatiors. Sorcery CAN come from making these bargen's, but their magic should be in the words and the friends they make. Their most basic Caste ability - to solidify a deal between two parties - is VERY exploitable. Just as the symbol and what they represent, they are about unifying forces - not casting spells to demand change. They are tricksters and manipulators. Not Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind these are FAVORED abilities. Not exclusive. Any Caste (even a Thuggish Dawn) can learn Occult and become a Spell Caster. This is desined to assign personality and purpose to each caste, and to match what they represent. If you can explain how the image of a Sunset and an Overlapping-of-Celestial-Bodies symbolize &quot;magical power&quot; in the way Sorcery behaves in Exalted, please do.<br /> <br /> But regardless, thats my opinion on where I'd like Exalted 3.5 to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154293#post1154293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you could just tell us which bits are giving you difficulty, and we can help you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The difficulty is the effort required to play the game and explain things to my group. Exalted takes an EFFORT to learn the rules and, in our current society, unless you are a complete geek - Exalted will intimidate many players away once they hit the Charm selection of the book.<br /> <br /> To learn how many Charms work, you need to learn how Combat works. And given many RPG players have come from DnD, where each fight round is typically 2-3 dice rolls at most (one roll to hit, one roll to wound), its a MASSIVE change when you have to understand the difference between Withering and Decisive, book keeping initiative order, book keeping motes spent, book keeping anima banner level, book keeping location, making the choice between Dodge or Parry, know the rules about grapples, clashes, etc...<br /> <br /> And thats at its simple. THEN if someone wants to go into Craft or Sorcery, you have to re-read the ENTIRE chapter on each of these to understand what Gold Points are, Silver Points, Sorcery Motes, rituals, Sorcerous Workings, etc... which again, unless you are a nerd who WANTS to learn this, you'll shut down fast.<br /> <br /> In the game we attempted, one player asked if they could take the Wyld Shaping Charms at the start of the game. By my calculations, they were allowed to. And that single charm required 3 pages to explain ONE ability!<br /> <br /> And THEN, even if you get through all the rules, you still need to understand the backstory of Exalted, what is a Deathlord, what is a Rashaka, how a God is a Spirit but how a Spirit is not an Elemental, etc...<br /> <br /> AND THEN, even if you get past ALLLL of that for character creation, when a player says they want to persuade a Guard to let them in the gate, the Gamemaster is confronted with the ability choice of &quot;do they use Bureacracy, Socialize, Presence, or Performance?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is comming from someone who has read the rules 3+ times, and understands it enough to make sense of it, but its just unneseccary headache as far as I can see. Even one of the most complicated Character Creation systems, the HERO system, still keeps combat fairly simple - &quot;roll X dice to hit, roll Y dice to wound, deal Z damage to target minus their resistance level&quot;.<br /> <br /> I respect Exalted is not a casual game, but it goes from Complicated to almost requiring a University Lecture to explain its basics. And the disapointment is that its world is great, but the mechanics prevent people getting in.<br /> <br /> Like other groups I've heard of, I've been tempted to just have my group explore the world of Creation using DnD rules or even the FATE Core system. Those mechanics are easy enough to use, though in doing so it would also drop a lot of what Exalted's characters could do.<br /> <br /> So if you can offer a way to streamline the entire mechanical sprawl of Exalted, make the whole thing less intimidating to players, accelerate the process that combat occurs, and give complete clarity on all the abilities so no one has any room to second guess &quot;why can't I use Athletics to Throw this Knife as an attack?&quot;, then I'd appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T03:23:07-07:00","id":1154325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154317#post1154317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Zenith getting Occult, I think its fine. And your statement of &quot;seriously&quot; doesn't give me any grounds to reply to your objection. So to respond to you and Hakkonen, my thinking behind it was that the Zenith are &quot;BIG&quot;. They are designed to be SEEN. Like the Sun at its peak, people notice them. So their actions are BIG. Nation shaking. They rally crowds into riots, or organize them into Armies. They manipulate energy that reshapes landscapes, devistates nations, changes the history books, etc... They are BIG. Their actions are ground shaking. It ties into their connection to their God - and as living champions of the sun, they use this power to bring change. Sometimes even directed by the UCS itself.<br /> <br /> As for why the Twilight and Eclipse loose this, its because thematically these two work in a different direction. The Twilight are still big, but their epic creations are physical. They create weapons, warstriders, fortresses, temples, Manses, armors, tools. Their magic exists in the Forge and the Pen. Their structure is more defensive, which comes from the theme of the Light Fading, and them fortifying their homes to survive the darkness until the Light comes. Sorcery is almost typically offensive, so it worked against the Twilight Theme.<br /> <br /> And the Eclipse are Deal Makers and Negotiatiors. Sorcery CAN come from making these bargen's, but their magic should be in the words and the friends they make. Their most basic Caste ability - to solidify a deal between two parties - is VERY exploitable. Just as the symbol and what they represent, they are about unifying forces - not casting spells to demand change. They are tricksters and manipulators. Not Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind these are FAVORED abilities. Not exclusive. Any Caste (even a Thuggish Dawn) can learn Occult and become a Spell Caster. This is desined to assign personality and purpose to each caste, and to match what they represent. If you can explain how the image of a Sunset and an Overlapping-of-Celestial-Bodies symbolize &quot;magical power&quot; in the way Sorcery behaves in Exalted, please do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, there's your problem. Sorcery is far from the only, or even primary, purview of Occult. To put it in your own terms:<br /> <br /> Occult is the ability for dealing with the esoteric, the uncanny, and the subtle powers of Creation. It is the ability that lets you stand in the gathering darkness and master the things that dwell there, or ward them away. It is the ability that lets you speak with gods and devils as equals, and step into the unknown without fear. Through Occult, you can force a mighty spirit to take shape before your eyes, learn the secret arts of the dead, and slip into the soul of an unhuman monster to commune with it in ways no one ever has (I've done exactly that, by the way, as an Eclipse).<br /> <br /> Occult is the ability of the exorcist, the shaman, and the scholar of the unknown, before it is the ability of the sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 10-31-2017, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T03:48:50-07:00","id":1154330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154325#post1154325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Occult is the ability for dealing with the esoteric, the uncanny, and the subtle powers of Creation. It is the ability that lets you stand in the gathering darkness and master the things that dwell there, or ward them away. It is the ability that lets you speak with gods and devils as equals, and step into the unknown without fear. Through Occult, you can force a mighty spirit to take shape before your eyes, learn the secret arts of the dead, and slip into the soul of an unhuman monster to commune with it in ways no one ever has (I've done exactly that, by the way, as an Eclipse).<br /> <br /> Occult is the ability of the exorcist, the shaman, and the scholar of the unknown, before it is the ability of the sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is how Occult works, then I still think it feels stronger at home with a Zenith who stands above all others and looks down on them, then a twilight who reflects when hope has faded and night/ death has come, or an Eclipse who unites two powers together to be something different - if even for a moment.<br /> <br /> If I go through your description (which I do like btw), and I were to assign abilities to each action, this would be what I'd suggest be the ability used:<br /> <br /> To Stand against the Darkness (Vigor) and master that which dwells there (Presence), or ward them away (Presence). Speak with Gods/ Devils as Equals (Bargen/Presence/ Lore), step into the unknown without fear (Willpower). Force a mighty spirit to take shape before your eyes (Presence), learn the secret arts of the dead (Lore/Occult), slip into the soul of an inhuman monster (Wildlife/ Perception/ Occult).<br /> <br /> I can see Occult being used for Thurmaturgy, and rituals would be needed to perform some more exotic acts, but a lot of what was described here feels like it could be used in other Abilities.<br /> <br /> Not rejecting the idea of a Twilight/ Eclipse studying the Occult. But still not convinced they should be &quot;iconic&quot; for the role of mystics given their intended purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T04:04:24-07:00","id":1154332,"title":"","content":"Twilights are, like, archetypal wizards. Their anima abilities are geared towards this and, remember, the greatest feats of artifice also require sorcery. In creation, technology <i>is</i> magic. Twilights not getting Occult, the ability of &quot;understand magic&quot; is just wrong on a fundamental level. <br /> <br /> Zeniths are Priest Kings. That's their thing. They can get sorcery to supplement this, but it's not really the main thrust of their theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T04:22:23-07:00","id":1154334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154332#post1154332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilights are, like, archetypal wizards. Their anima abilities are geared towards this and, remember, the greatest feats of artifice also require sorcery. In creation, technology <i>is</i> magic. Twilights not getting Occult, the ability of &quot;understand magic&quot; is just wrong on a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> Zeniths are Priest Kings. That's their thing. They can get sorcery to supplement this, but it's not really the main thrust of their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are missing my point - What is it about Twilight, the setting of the sun, that symbolizes Sorcery?<br /> <br /> I respect what the Twilight are/were in all editions - but this is looking at the game not for what it was, but what it could be. How can the Castes represent what they symbolize.<br /> <br /> My variation encourages a Twilight as the time of reflecting on what has been to find new ways forward - much like how you can reflect at the end of the day on all that you've done, and plan for tomorrow. The Twilight are about reflecting on the past to make things better later - and my skill assignment does this. They build objects to improve the future/ rebuild what once was, they cure illnesses that have ran rampant, they educate people to be enlightened, the observe at a distance to think about how to proceed next.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;this is what Twilight are/ have always been&quot; is fine. You can like what they have always been. But equally I can say they can be more accurate to what they were designed to be.<br /> <br /> Saying its &quot;wrong on a fundamenetal level&quot; offers no grounds to persuade. It only states you are passionate about how things are, and don't want them to change. Which they won't. This isn't an official mod. Its a fan made opinion on what could be.<br /> <br /> If you cannot look at things in a different light, and cling to just what things are, there is little point in me responding to your comments as you've really offered nothing worth challenging my ideas.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":5915,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","user":"zenvious","date":". 10-31-2017, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T04:22:23-07:00","id":1154335,"title":"","content":"deleted duplicate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T04:52:31-07:00","id":1154339,"title":"","content":"Twilights <i>know stuff</i>. Makers, thinkers, doers. That's right in the description. Occult is, first and foremost, an ability about <i>knowing stuff</i>. About delving into the unknown. That's twilight as fuck.<br /> <br /> It's also required for creating artifacts. Twilights need to have <i>every</i> ability associated with creating artifacts as caste. Come on, that's just obvious. You don't need occult supernal to be a sorcerer, it doesn't help. But you need it at least favoured to be a proper articifer. And &quot;Ability you basically <i>need</i> to do your thing&quot; is pretty much the definition of a caste ability. <br /> <br /> Also &quot;What is it about Twilight, the setting of the sun, that symbolizes Sorcery?&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, Everything? That's been a thing since forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:04:50-07:00","id":1154343,"title":"","content":"I must agree that if any Caste should get Occult exclusively, it's the Twilight, not the Zenith. If you want to completely redefine the purpose and lore of the Castes, that's fine, but realize that you've gone somewhere where this forum can't really help you.<br /> <br /> The importance of the Occult ability to the Castes, in decreasing order:<br /> <br /> 1) Twilight - Uh, 'sorcerer' is a core concept of the caste. And they can bind demons with a caste ability. <br /> 2) Eclipse - They have to deal with the spirits in their own area. This makes it very important to have Occult.<br /> 3) Zenith - Rulers should know about the people they rule. At least somewhat.<br /> 4) Night - If spirits go rogue, who deals with them?<br /> 5) Dawn - Someone has to be last.<br /> <br /> I think if you do this for each Ability, they will naturally sort themselves.<br /> <br /> Also, is there any reason you simply... eliminated Linguistics and Integrity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:21:55-07:00","id":1154347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154339#post1154339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilights <i>know stuff</i>. Makers, thinkers, doers. That's right in the description. Occult is, first and foremost, an ability about <i>knowing stuff</i>. About delving into the unknown. That's twilight as fuck.<br /> <br /> It's also required for creating artifacts. Twilights need to have <i>every</i> ability associated with creating artifacts as caste. Come on, that's just obvious. You don't need occult supernal to be a sorcerer, it doesn't help. But you need it at least favoured to be a proper articifer. And &quot;Ability you basically <i>need</i> to do your thing&quot; is pretty much the definition of a caste ability.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;What is it about Twilight, the setting of the sun, that symbolizes Sorcery?&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, Everything? That's been a thing since forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I appreciate your effort Elfive, you continue to keep missing the point I am asking. You are talking as if this should be self explanatory, and its not. So, as I have said, while I appreciate your attempt to offer insight - you continue to offer nothing I can respond to, nor anything that convinces me to think otherwise.<br /> <br /> Thus, if it continues, I won't be responding to anything you say regarding this if your future comments continue the pattern of &quot;Its fine as is - you can't/shouldn't change anything&quot; if there is no rational reasoning behind your statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":5915,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","user":"zenvious","date":". 10-31-2017, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:33:53-07:00","id":1154348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154343#post1154343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must agree that if any Caste should get Occult exclusively, it's the Twilight, not the Zenith. If you want to completely redefine the purpose and lore of the Castes, that's fine, but realize that you've gone somewhere where this forum can't really help you.<br /> <br /> The importance of the Occult ability to the Castes, in decreasing order:<br /> <br /> 1) Twilight - Uh, 'sorcerer' is a core concept of the caste. And they can bind demons with a caste ability.<br /> 2) Eclipse - They have to deal with the spirits in their own area. This makes it very important to have Occult.<br /> 3) Zenith - Rulers should know about the people they rule. At least somewhat.<br /> 4) Night - If spirits go rogue, who deals with them?<br /> 5) Dawn - Someone has to be last.<br /> <br /> I think if you do this for each Ability, they will naturally sort themselves.<br /> <br /> Also, is there any reason you simply... eliminated Linguistics and Integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div>A valid point and direction, though again I've never said its exclusive to the Zenith but rather they are Legendary in using it. However I suspect people have gotten far too fixated on the Occult point, and I suspect its because I cannot see how people are seeing Occult - while my view of it is to have it used for General Knowledge of the Supernatural (while Lore is knowledge of the &quot;natural&quot;). Anything involving negotiating with a Spirit (such as an Eclipse) would be a challenge to be met with an interactive skill - such as Performance, Bureacracy, Socialize - as those are the interactive skills. Occult won't let you persuade the creature, but it may let you understand what it is - and by understanding it maybe you will get a benefit in your negotiations.<br /> <br /> For me I see Occult as the opposite of Lore. Lore deals with the Academics of the world (history, literature, human culture, maths, science, mundane knowledge). Occult deals with the supernatural (knowledge of gods, daemons, spirits, elementals, rituals, sorcery). For me I see it as an Academic VS a Priest. Its different fields of knowledge, but inevitably its knowledge based more than practical application (though that knowledge can LEAD to practical application).<br /> <br /> You may be right that the forum may not have anything to offer. This was more of a &quot;here's an idea to consider&quot;, and you actually have helped me Ulthwithian - your nudge definately helped me merged Bureacracy and Socialize. Feels a bit better too!<br /> <br /> As for your new question - no linguistics and integrity - this was because I felt both were semi redundant.<br /> <br /> Linguistics was more of a filler ability than an active skill. The ability to talk privately would be covered by Socialize, to talk to crowds would be covered by Presence, to write a letter would come also under Socilaize but could be bridged slightly with Lore (playing on the Academic idea of that ability). Inevitably I felt the ability was made to give reason to learn new languages; which for me felt more like a Perk than a skill as far as mechanic go. Hence my discarding of it.<br /> <br /> Integrity was similar - I felt Willpower covered a lot of those rolls. And the Charms could find homes in other places (such as Resistance).<br /> <br /> In fact Linguistics was the original skill I dismissed which got me onto the whole idea of wondering how many skills WERE redundant as far as this game was concerned!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:43:54-07:00","id":1154349,"title":"","content":"That last post was an attempt to unpack my reasoning, but obviously an unsuccessful one. <br /> <br /> Basically, look at it this way: Twilights are artifact makers, right? That's their major thing. But to make an artifact you need Occult 3. <br /> <br /> So to do their thing, a Twilight <i>needs </i>to have Occult. Are you with me so far? Even <i>aside</i> from the &quot;Twilights are Wizards&quot; thing, which would swing it for me on it's own, the <i>other</i> major Twilight avenue, the one that's not in dispute at all, <i>also</i> requires Occult. <br /> <br /> If an Exalt caste <i>needs</i> to have an ability to do their major thing, then I posit that that ability <i>has</i> to be a caste ability. That's what caste abilities <i>are. </i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:59:25-07:00","id":1154352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154349#post1154349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last post was an attempt to unpack my reasoning, but obviously an unsuccessful one.<br /> <br /> Basically, look at it this way: Twilights are artifact makers, right? That's their major thing. But to make an artifact you need Occult 3.<br /> <br /> So to do their thing, a Twilight <i>needs </i>to have Occult. Are you with me so far? Even <i>aside</i> from the &quot;Twilights are Wizards&quot; thing, which would swing it for me on it's own, the <i>other</i> major Twilight avenue, the one that's not in dispute at all, <i>also</i> requires Occult.<br /> <br /> If an Exalt caste <i>needs</i> to have an ability to do their major thing, then I posit that that ability <i>has</i> to be a caste ability. That's what caste abilities <i>are. </i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats a fair argument! And I appreciate that you explained it. It makes sense from where you are comming from.<br /> <br /> My retort is - why should they have Occult 3? Why not just a high enough Craft? Why not Craft Charms that allows you to imbue your own Essence into the Magical Metal/ Materials you are working with to make a badass artifact? Why is Occult required beyond the point of &quot;because thats how it is in the rule books?&quot;<br /> <br /> The way I'd see it is that a Mortal with Craft 5 can make a Big sword. They can even make a Big sword out of Jade. And it &quot;may&quot; be an Artifact weapon, but for the most part its just a large item made of a particular metal (real world comparison). Its the limit of what a Mortal could produce.<br /> <br /> An Exalt with the same Craft score could imbue mundane material (steel, wood) with their Essence in its creation to create a 'mundane' Artifact weapon which may have unique properties, but still not be at &quot;Artifact level&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or the same Exalt could do the same object, but working with Magical Materials, make a powerful weapon/ armor/ warstrider etc. The fact the Exalted can use Essence to empower an object should be magic enough - Occult isn't required for it to happen. Being able to inject Essence into an object should be mystical. Occult should be something seperate to it.<br /> <br /> I can see the argument being &quot;for a weapon to be enchanted, one must understand enchantment&quot; but for me - it feels like more complexity for little overall purpose. You want to build something? Use Craft. Simple. You want to cast Sorcery? Use Occult. Simple.<br /> <br /> I know some Artifacts have high magical qualities, but I've seen that more as a comination of the craftsman skill to mold the material to a result - not from casting Enchantment INTO the material once its complete. Sorcery is large and visable. Craft is subtle and precise. The two do cross paths, but they are unique qualities.<br /> <br /> Thats what my mind is on. My proposal doesn't prevent you being both - just makes things simple to be more inviting to casual players; less confusion creates less conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T06:56:29-07:00","id":1154363,"title":"","content":"It would seem your issue is that you view Occult as 'non-academic', or basically a Mysticism Ability which is inherently non-rational, and Twilights as 'the rational ones'.<br /> <br /> Skipping over the fact that this is not even true <i>in the real world</i>, I feel that you are reading a popular if inaccurate real-world theory into Creation. Spirits exist. Occult is far closer to xenobiology than parapsychology here. Salt rings deterring spirits is a <i>scientific fact</i> in Creation, not a superstition. And Occult is the Ability that says you know not only that salt rings deter spirits, you know why.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I feel that you are viewing Occult as 'the Ability that people who sacrifice goats use because they don't know any better use', when--especially from a Solar perspective--it's closer to a Hermetic mage or a scientific view of astrology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:20:51-07:00","id":1154367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154363#post1154363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would seem your issue is that you view Occult as 'non-academic', or basically a Mysticism Ability which is inherently non-rational, and Twilights as 'the rational ones'.<br /> <br /> Skipping over the fact that this is not even true <i>in the real world</i>, I feel that you are reading a popular if inaccurate real-world theory into Creation. Spirits exist. Occult is far closer to xenobiology than parapsychology here. Salt rings deterring spirits is a <i>scientific fact</i> in Creation, not a superstition. And Occult is the Ability that says you know not only that salt rings deter spirits, you know why.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I feel that you are viewing Occult as 'the Ability that people who sacrifice goats use because they don't know any better use', when--especially from a Solar perspective--it's closer to a Hermetic mage or a scientific view of astrology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite. My view is its more Occult is the Knowledge Skill of the Supernatural Forces (Ghosts, Elementals, Spirits, Gods, Sorcery). Killing Goats CAN be used in Occult, but higher Occult would let you know the process required to benefit from the Sacrifice. I am in agreement it is about Hermetic Mages and Astrology, and when Essence uses it, the results can be huge. But even a Mortal can have high enough Occult to know about the Salt Ring. It is a Scientific FACT, but that knowledge would only be available to those who study that area - its the equivilant of having studied Biology, but not knowing anything Psychology. Different fields, but both come under knowledge and study.<br /> <br /> Creation does know Spirits Exist. Gods Exist. Their entire society exists on that principal, and its VERY unlikely any Adult Mortal has lived without encountering a Spirit at least once in some regard (even if seen at a distance). These are known facts. I'm not arguing that.<br /> <br /> But someone with low Occult may mistake an Exalted for a God, while someone with high Occult would know that its an Exalted, and also what &quot;force&quot; Exalted them, AND what their Caste is.<br /> <br /> Someone with low Occult may make the error of throwing Salt at an Exalted, or making a Salt ring to protect themselves, only to find it failed. Which in turn would lead them to assume their &quot;Salt Protects against Spirits&quot; is wrong information. When, in reality, their information on protection was correct - they just used it on the wrong thing because they lacked the ability to know what it was the were facing.<br /> <br /> Someone with Lore on the otherhand may make the God-confusion in the same scenario, but could probably identify the person's origin by their clothing and accent - something Occult would not bother to focus on or even know. They may even be confused as to why a Southern Spirit has come soo far northwards - and may jump to assumptions of which God it is they are seeing, which could lead to further confusion and conflict. Again, their information may be right, but the field of study is wrong.<br /> <br /> Thats how I view it. Both skills have practical application for information gathering.<br /> <br /> But again, since the Zenith have a direct tie to their God (tUCS), it makes more sense that they would have a better knowledge of dealing with similar forces. Or that they would gain the tricks to seal such entities (aka take the Twilight abilities). And, visually, it makes sense that the full power of the Sun would humble such targets. Standing above them, looking down on them cowaring. The Twilight image doesn't give me that - a Sunset is a Solar retreating to think and work unseen does shout &quot;pins spirits down&quot;. At best it leads them to taking Spirits away and Interrogating them behind closed doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":5915,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","user":"zenvious","date":". 10-31-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:38:06-07:00","id":1154371,"title":"","content":"I think you're taking the caste names a little too literally. You just described Occult as a knowledge ability, but then said that a caste whose <i>entire shtick is knowing shit</i> has less justification for having it as a a caste ability than another caste whose expertise lies in a totally different direction. <br /> <br /> Zenith's don't have any more of a direct line to Conky than any other solar. They get a pep talk when they exalt. That's it. They're not the mystics - that's twilight. They don't <i>understand</i> the spirits. That's twilight. <br /> <br /> You're getting such a push back against this because Occult is <i>fundamental</i> to the twilight caste identity. Saying they shouldn't get it it like saying a Night shouldn't get Stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:52:38-07:00","id":1154374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154371#post1154371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're taking the caste names a little too literally. You just described Occult as a knowledge ability, but then said that a caste whose <i>entire shtick is knowing shit</i> has less justification for having it as a a caste ability than another caste whose expertise lies in a totally different direction.<br /> <br /> Zenith's don't have any more of a direct line to Conky than any other solar. They get a pep talk when they exalt. That's it. They're not the mystics - that's twilight. They don't <i>understand</i> the spirits. That's twilight.<br /> <br /> You're getting such a push back against this because Occult is <i>fundamental</i> to the twilight caste identity. Saying they shouldn't get it it like saying a Night shouldn't get Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And why should I NOT take the Caste names literally? Elfive you did great in your previous comment, giving a nice justification and explaination, but you seem to have gone straight back to your strategy of discouraging me from continuing to express an idea and be creative. I'll overlook it and focus instead on the parts that seem worth responding to for the sake of this thread.<br /> <br /> Yes the Zenith get a pep talk at Exaltation but.... why NOT more? Why shouldn't they get more Spiritual Guidance? Why not make the UCS a common mentor for many Zenith - or give them an anima ability that lets them get visions in the form of the Sun trying to assign his chosen missions? Why not expand on an idea that works and has potential to be more.<br /> <br /> My statement regarding the Twilight was they REFLECT on knowledge - not that they KNOW stuff. They find solutions to problems.<br /> <br /> Further, Night Castes SHOULD have Stealth. Night is the Absence of the Sun. They should be almost direct Opposites of the Zenith. So naturally they SHOULD have Stealth. Zenith is the Sun at its peak. Their actions SHOULD be big and visable. Twilight is the Sun leaving to rest, isolate itself into private effort, or hide from danger. Their actions SHOULD be suggestive of subtle and unseen preparedness to be unleashed come the Dawn.<br /> <br /> And sure I'm getting a push back. But at least when <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian\">Ulthwithian</a></b> offers a counter, its productive and questioning. I've gained valuable inspiration from him challenging me. All you've done is show me that people are stubborn, don't want to think outside the box, and get passionately objective when their comfort zone is challenged.<br /> <br /> Point is, I accept push back as, if I can defend my point well enough, it means that I'm on to something right. So if you want to oppose my idea, give me rational reason with mechanical and thematic evidence that supports your approach - instead of just saying &quot;its always been that way - accept it&quot;. I don't accept it.<br /> <br /> Much like a Twilight, I am seeing a problem, and am seeking a solution to overcome it.<br /> <br /> Your approach seems very Dawn - if faced with a problem, hit it with a hammer enough times or intimidate it until it goes away. Its kinda cardboard cutout and boring TBH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T08:13:27-07:00","id":1154376,"title":"","content":"They find solutions to problems, yeah, but <i>that's what occult is for</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble arguing my point because you keep taking what I see as arguments <i>for</i> twilight getting occult and presenting them as if they point <i>away</i> from it. Zeniths are leaders. They see the big picture, and they command spirits with force of personality and rhetoric. They don't delve in, find metaphysical strings and tug. Technical stuff like that is about understanding. About getting your hands dirty.<br /> <br /> The capstone charm in the occult tree lets you stitch together a bunch of spirits you've absorbed into a new one. Does that sound more Zenith or Twilight to you? Craft: Genesis is the purview of sorcerous workings now. Does Dr Frankenstein seem more like a Twilight or a Zenith?<br /> <br /> Maybe I could give you a better argument for why I think Twilight should get Occult rather than Zeniths if I could wrap my head around why the <i>hell</i> anyone would suggest otherwise.<br /> <br /> Everything else is fine, by the way. It's a pretty good idea. I just get to the Occult thing and I'm just &quot;Wait, hold the fuck up. What?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-31-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T08:47:17-07:00","id":1154392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154376#post1154376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They find solutions to problems, yeah, but <i>that's what occult is for</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble arguing my point because you keep taking what I see as arguments <i>for</i> twilight getting occult and presenting them as if they point <i>away</i> from it. Zeniths are leaders. They see the big picture, and they command spirits with force of personality and rhetoric. They don't delve in, find metaphysical strings and tug. Technical stuff like that is about understanding. About getting your hands dirty.<br /> <br /> The capstone charm in the occult tree lets you stitch together a bunch of spirits you've absorbed into a new one. Does that sound more Zenith or Twilight to you? Craft: Genesis is the purview of sorcerous workings now. Does Dr Frankenstein seem more like a Twilight or a Zenith?<br /> <br /> Maybe I could give you a better argument for why I think Twilight should get Occult rather than Zeniths if I could wrap my head around why the <i>hell</i> anyone would suggest otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well lets see if we can find some clarity. The basis of my argument is based of a few principals:<br /> <br /> 1) The overall goal is to simplify the selection of abilities down - reducing it (currently) from 25/26 abilities, down to 16 abilities, to make things simpler and more streamlined<br /> 2) Each Exalt should have both Exclusively Favored Abilities, and Shared Favored Abilities, to again make things simpler (less abilities means less book keeping and less research needed)<br /> 3) If possible, the Icon/ Symbol of the Caste should dictate their role - not each Caste should have a Role and their Icon be assigned to represent said role (aka - it should be Sunset represents Sorcery, not Sorcery is represented by a Sunset/ Eclipse).<br /> 4) Due to this being a fan-made suggestion with no offical weight - the idea should be free roaming and not constrained by pre-existing mechanics (Charms, Anima Effects) or game history (Twilight have always been the archetype Sorcerers).<br /> <br /> So this isn't a challenge of saying Exalted is bad. Its a proposal that it could be something different, while still similar, taking what are good qualities, but editing the rest to try and build it towards something better - but equally making it simpler and more accessable.<br /> <br /> So if we go through this one at a time, maybe you can see where I'm comming from. And then maybe you can give insight in a way that encourages me to see your view, so we can finally achieve clarity:<br /> <br /> 1) Many skills have been Merged Down. Brawl is now merged into Melee (basically close-combat fighting), Dodge and &quot;part&quot; of Athletics are merged into Acrobatics, Resilience and &quot;part&quot; of Atheletics are Merged into Vigor, etc... pulling 25 abilities down by 9 into 16 abilities, so that with less Abilities to choose from, the Storyteller won't need overthink things to figure out which ability is needed for what test attempt.<br /> <br /> 2) My chart has designed this &quot;2 Exclusive Favored, 3 Shared Favored&quot; setup. So far the major resistance I've had has been on the basis of Zenith getting Occult, and Twilight and Eclipse losing it. However, it seems my other proposed ideas of shared Lore, Perception, Acrobatics, Vigor, and War seem to have been accepted without major issue. So the issue seems to lie more in the basis of &quot;why Occult there and not elsewhere?&quot; In which, case offer a proposal of where you think Occult SHOULD go, and what the Zenith should gain instead, and why.<br /> <br /> 3) I've reviewed the Icons of the Castes and looked at what they could represent, and this in turn encourages the abilities each Caste should get for what they represent. My view in this variation, to try to match their icons, are as follows:<ul><li>Dawn - They push back the Night/ Darkness/ Evil/ Enemy. People Run from them. They are Dangerous. They are Killers. They are power. They make things Go Away - through active Execution or threat of doing so.</li> <li>Zenith - They Stand Tall and are seen by all. They Command and are Obeyed. They are the closest to Heaven then any other in their Group, and are connected to the Gods the Govern all by their height. Enemies are humbled by them. Mortals bask in their Glory and feel no fear as their world is illuminated. Nothing is hidden from their height.</li> <li>Twilight - They Watch for Incomming Threats (the approaching Darkness that ends the Light), and find solutions to survive the attack. They do not retreat or hide, but rather remove themselves to create solutions to problems. They do not Command, but they offer support and Wisdom and Councilers. They reflect on what has been.</li> <li>Night - They maintain Hope when Darkness has engulfed all. They are present even if unseen. They manipulate the world, but are ignored when doing so. They attack and vanish before their victim or witness knew they were ever there. They are the scouts that let the shadows know the light is comming back.</li> <li>Eclipse - They unite forces, make enemies into friends, make deals between parties, resolve conflicts with words and discussion, they appear and do their part and then leave just as suddenly leaving a strong emotional memory and a longing for it to return. They are mysterious and yet known. They are the unifers who bring peace with diplomacy.</li> </ul>Each of these descriptions play to the image of the State the Sun is in each time. Ignoring what the Caste Abilities have been, do these descriptions fit the idea of what this Sun State could be? And if so, why don't we make the abilities fit THESE descriptions?<br /> <br /> 4) If all of this worked, it would lead to redesigning entire Charm Trees for each Ability, and reviewing Anima Effects for similar results. But, if it did work (and I feel it DOES work), the Icons of the Sun would fit more comfortably with their abilities, instead of just being placeholder titles for each role being &quot;Warrior, Paladin, Mage, Rogue, Bard&quot; which I feel all versions of Exalted kinda have been.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The big reason i offer this is, I had hopes 3rd Ed might make headway from what the previous editions were. 1st was ok, 2nd became more complicated, and I had issues with both their mechanical designs. 3rd had been my hope it would repair itself, and when I was disapointed I decide &quot;screw it - if they won't make the game I feel this world COULD be, I'll quit complaining about it and get to work in making my own Exalted version. Something that could meet what I feel are some of its flaws - specifically being too convoluted for casuals to join in. And, if simplifying things down requires me to tweak the Lore designs of the games Legacy, so be it! The game is going to be different regardless - maybe THIS difference may be appealing!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T09:38:54-07:00","id":1154410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154392#post1154392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the issue seems to lie more in the basis of &quot;why Occult there and not elsewhere?&quot; In which, case offer a proposal of where you think Occult SHOULD go, and what the Zenith should gain instead, and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, for starters switch out sail for occult in the twilight. Seriously, you took Occult and gave them <i>Sail?</i> How is Sail more of a Twilight ability than Occult?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this has the knock-on effect that Occult is no longer exclusive, and Sail is. This is a bit trickier, because swapping Occult for any of the eclipse exclusives could be an issue. Socialize might work, but Eclipse need it and, honestly, so do Night Castes. It's the &quot;hide intentions&quot; ability, and there's a lot of stuff in there that's useful for them. But there's no real place to put it. We could give dawn back full control of one of the combat abilities, but then they'd end up with three exclusives and we're back to step 1.<br /> <br /> Also Dawn should probably have Acrobatics. Evasion is pretty important for a brawler.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I got so caught up on the occult thing that I never really noticed it's just the capstone on a bunch of other problems here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-31-2017, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:04:00-07:00","id":1154424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154410#post1154410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, for starters switch out sail for occult in the twilight. Seriously, you took Occult and gave them <i>Sail?</i> How is Sail more of a Twilight ability than Occult?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this has the knock-on effect that Occult is no longer exclusive, and Sail is. This is a bit trickier, because swapping Occult for any of those could be an issue. Socialize might work, but Eclipse need it and, honestly, so do Night Castes. It's the &quot;hide intentions&quot; ability, and there's a lot of stuff in there that's useful for them. But there's no real place to put it. We could give dawn back full control of one of the combat abilities, but then they'd end up with three exclusives and we're back to step 1.<br /> <br /> Also Dawn should probably have Acrobatics. Evasion is pretty important for a brawler.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I got so caught up on the occult thing that I never really noticed it's just the capstone on a bunch of other problems here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend drop the passive aggressive terminology where you are talking down to me. Instead how about you rephrase your opening to &quot;Could you explain how you saw Sail as a more Twilight Ability than Occult?&quot; It invites the person to explain themselves, instead of being demanded to justify their position.<br /> <br /> As for Sail, if you'd read the other posts (and not just the ones you've replied to) you'd noticed in my second Chart I cut Sail out as well - merging its affects into other Abilities. The book even said that Sail is an ability that the chapter will either revolve around, or be ignored. So cutting it worked well towards stream lining.<br /> <br /> Socialize should be a skill for creating deals and manipulating others - NOT be the defense to such attempts. As a social defense I'd probably make it Willpower Related, but again that's going into Mechanical territory which I just clarified this is NOT focusing on.<br /> <br /> Dawn already has 2 out of the 3/4 (if you consider War) of the Combat abilities. Giving them all 3 sounds stubborn and unimaginative. And there is no logical reason why Thrown should be Dawn Exclusive. Thrown is more of an improvised combat skill than a Glorious Champion technique. That fits perfectly for a Night Caste whose Combat style should be Ambush encouraged - and Throwing weapons are idea for Social Ambushes (a bow is a tad obvious).<br /> <br /> And there is no reason why Dawn should have Athletics. Vigor designs them to resist damage - takin a hit and shruging it off like its no big deal is FAR more intimidating than a nimble dodging ninja.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I appreciate your effort, but personally I don't think you are ever going to see what I am suggesting here. Your approach continues to feel you are not open to mods, and are doing your best to discourage any suggested change from your comfort zone of what the game is/was. If you can't be open to the possibility the game as it is has issues, then you won't ever see them even when presented to you. And your arrogance of tone, and condessending choice of words, are highly encouraging that I cease giving you any effort as it feels trying to explain this to you further would be a lost cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:25:13-07:00","id":1154432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities#post1154067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- merged some of the pre-existing abilities for mechanical streamlining</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think Exalted's ability spread is bad, take a look at GURPS :-P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities#post1154067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- shared favored abilities around more (aka no more &quot;you can only choose Archery as your Supernal ability if you are Dawn Caste&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this is pretty much why supernal abilities was introduced in the first place. To make sure that each caste actually had a niche in which only they can shine. You're basically just eroding the actual distinctions between the castes. This was a huge problem in 2E where if you wanted to build the most impressive fighter, you couldn't use the dawn caste. Any backsliding to that standard I view as a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities#post1154067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spread gives each Caste two exclusively favored Abilities (see the first two emboldened columns), and gives each Caste at least either Vigor or Acrobatics for a defensive ability (Vigor for toughening out damage, Acrobatics for avoiding it).</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes no sense. Defending against stuff isn't a core part of every caste. This is why you can always choose something as a favoured ability. Caste abilities should emphasize what that caste does best, not what you think should be covered in a 'build.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities#post1154067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also an ability bridge into each Caste - Dawn and Zenith both have War, Zenith and Twilight both have Lore, Twilight and Night both have Perception, and Night and Dawn have Archery AND Thrown. This is slightly for flavor, giving the feel that each Caste Flows into the next (Eclipse is the exception, though they share Sail with Twilight, and Wildlife with the Zenith).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you've got 5 abilities in each caste, I'm assuming you've gone back to 2E's idea of 5 caste abilities that have no variance. And from your other comments I surmise that you've done away with the additional 5 favoured abilities you'd get to choose beyond your caste abilities.<br /> <br /> Did you also note that without changing the charms overly much that you've given the following breakdown of charm trees out: <br /> <br /> Dawn - 5.5<br /> Zenith - 5.5<br /> Twilight - 6<br /> Night - 5.5<br /> Eclipse - 7 <br /> <br /> While Linguistics and Integrity are just... gone. Oh hey, You could add linguistics back in to the Eclipse caste since they're all about travel and deal making. Except that'd give them access to 2 full charm trees more than anyone else so there's that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I agree character creation will need be adjusted with this. My idea is to go with characters choosing a Primary Supernal Ability, AND a Secondary Supernal Ability. The Primary must be from their Favored Ability (as listed), and they treat the purchasing of Charms for that Ability as if their Essence was +2 Higher (aka they can have up to Essence 3 Charms in that ability).<br /> <br /> The Secondary Ability can be ANY ability (not just the favored) and they treat charm purchase as if their Essence was +1 Higher (so they can have Essence 2 Charms for that Ability). It spreads the character creation options around for more interesting combos, while still encouraging theme of what your character is &quot;destined&quot; to be good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is supposed to <i>reduce</i> mechanical complexity?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:28:36-07:00","id":1154435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154424#post1154424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it feels trying to explain this to you further would be a lost cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I actually have to agree, We seem to disagree on what the core inviolate parts of the system should be. I'm open to changes, just... none of the ones you're proposing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T14:52:11-07:00","id":1154520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154424#post1154424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend drop the passive aggressive terminology where you are talking down to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be aware that you've been very condescending throughout this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T20:22:37-07:00","id":1154592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154374#post1154374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My statement regarding the Twilight was they REFLECT on knowledge - not that they KNOW stuff. They find solutions to problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then your statement is incorrect. The Twilight caste are the researchers, investigators, archivists, and librarians of the Solars. Scholarship - &quot;knowing stuff&quot; - is the core of the Twilight identity; this is why they're the only caste for whom Investigation, Lore, and Occult are all caste abilities. Twilight Solars, above all else, are seekers after knowledge. Frankly, your &quot;Twilights solve problems&quot; thing doesn't even make sense. All Solars solve problems; their caste is about how they approach their problems.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T20:52:12-07:00","id":1154602,"title":"","content":"Given the degree of toxicity this thread is starting to head towards, as most of the comments now are directed at trying to outright dismiss my idea, instead of offering constructive debate and brain storming (which had been my aspiring goal for offering my alternative). I will not be giving this thread any further effort.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the comments of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian\">Ulthwithian</a></b> who, at least, spoke with respectful terminology and was not dismissive. And even challenged my ideas to reconsider things, instead of criticizing the flaws of my ideas (which the majority seem fixated on doing - which by the way is easy. It takes no effort to say someone is wrong; but it takes a mature and wise mind to appreciate a creative effort to find an alternative solution). From his imput, I will take this as productive.<br /> <br /> To the rest, I have no interest in trying to justify my stance further. I have passionately tried to explain my vision, and have been met with dismissive arrogance. So I request this thread be locked, since there is clearly no point in me trying to discuss any creative direction with such closed minds.<br /> <br /> If anything I'll be taking shelter here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://groupthink.kinja.com/not-shocking-most-people-hate-creativity-but-say-other-1478416854\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://groupthink.kinja.com/not-shocking-most-people-hate-creativity-but-say-other-1478416854\" target=\"_blank\"> Vercel Security Checkpoint </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://groupthink.kinja.com/not-shocking-most-people-hate-creativity-but-say-other-1478416854\" target=\"_blank\"> http://groupthink.kinja.com/not-shocking-most-people-hate-creativity-but-say-other-1478416854 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.elitedaily.com/life/culture/people-understand-creative-people/929580\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://imgix.bustle.com/elite-daily/2015/08/06024206/Stocksy_txp362516cfqjW000_Small_201649.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=630&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces&amp;fm=jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.elitedaily.com/life/culture/people-understand-creative-people/929580\" target=\"_blank\"> 5 Traits Creative People Have That Most People Will Never Understand </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.elitedaily.com/life/culture/people-understand-creative-people/929580\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.elitedaily.com/life/culture/people-understand-creative-people/929580 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Creative people are troublemakers. They&rsquo;re druggies. They&rsquo;re slightly bonkers. And they usually dress funny... or so many of us would like to think. Creative people are, by definition, different. Of course, everyone in the world is a little&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":5915,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","user":"zenvious","date":". 11-01-2017, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T21:51:21-07:00","id":1154614,"title":"","content":"You know I was enjoying reading this thread and the differing viewpoints right up until the end. Saying in a huff &quot;Oh! Well you people just don't get it!&quot; only makes you feel immature, it's like getting the crap kicked out of you in a fight and going &quot;Well I let you win!&quot;<br /> <br /> I've had my works called shit before. I've had my work stolen before. But there is a world of difference between being able to take honest criticism that is attempting to reach the central point of your work vs needless browbeating. I've had some replies calling me things such as &quot;You are a fucking retard?&quot; or &quot;are you insane?&quot;, but I took their complaints and used it to better my work even if their tone was completely negative in nature and attacking me on a personal level.<br /> <br /> I was reading this thread casually while on the bus home so I can't weigh in on the finer points, but at least I can weigh in on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T22:16:41-07:00","id":1154619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154614#post1154614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I was enjoying reading this thread and the differing viewpoints right up until the end. Saying in a huff &quot;Oh! Well you people just don't get it!&quot; only makes you feel immature, it's like getting the crap kicked out of you in a fight and going &quot;Well I let you win!&quot;<br /> <br /> I've had my works called shit before. I've had my work stolen before. But there is a world of difference between being able to take honest criticism that is attempting to reach the central point of your work vs needless browbeating. I've had some replies calling me things such as &quot;You are a fucking retard?&quot; or &quot;are you insane?&quot;, but I took their complaints and used it to better my work even if their tone was completely negative in nature and attacking me on a personal level.<br /> <br /> I was reading this thread casually while on the bus home so I can't weigh in on the finer points, but at least I can weigh in on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there had been more comments that were inspiring me to pursue discussion of the topic, I'd have continued. But I am not going to waste my effort talking in a forum where the responses have primarily been aimed to dismiss my idea instead of offering constructive thought.<br /> <br /> As said, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian\">Ulthwithian</a></b> provided comment/ critique that allowed me to reduce my chart further by merging Socialize and Bureacracy. That progressed my work. But I have done more then enough effort to explain my view to <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\">Elfive</a></b> whose response has been to keep defending the core material, instead of considering an alternative, which is not what this thread was aimed to do.<br /> <br /> Since it was derailed, and further replies were equally dismissive, and unproductive, I saw no value of asking this forum for further feedback or giving it further effort if the results were just going to be continued wasted effort. Thus I decided if my creative efforts are going to be outright shut down by people with very little weight in their argument, I would make no further effort to entertain them.<br /> <br /> P.S.: if you had been enjoying my work, it would have been appreciated if you had spoken up on it earlier to give me encouragement to keep trying to debate it. When an individual is bombarded by 4+ people all suggesting the idea doesn't have merit, and knowing the idea will likely not be of any significant worth regardless of effort invested into it, its very discouraging to be alone without anyone to say &quot;I appreciate what you are trying here. Have you considered....?&quot; Its tiring, and with no fuel to keep going, the engine shuts down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":5915,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","user":"zenvious","date":". 11-01-2017, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T22:49:36-07:00","id":1154630,"title":"","content":"You're suffering from two issues:<br /> <br /> 1) You've got a solution in search of a problem. You said that the complexity of the rules and the difficulty explaining them is your main obstacle, but neither pruning Abilities nor reconceptualizing castes actually does anything for that.<br /> <br /> 2) The fact that your &quot;solution&quot; is unrelated to your &quot;problem,&quot; plus your own generally combative tone, makes me think you're just trolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T03:14:23-07:00","id":1154658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154602#post1154602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://groupthink.kinja.com/not-shocking-most-people-hate-creativity-but-say-other-1478416854\" target=\"_blank\">http://groupthink.kinja.com/not-shoc...her-1478416854</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.elitedaily.com/life/culture/people-understand-creative-people/929580\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.elitedaily.com/life/cult...-people/929580</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's start with a basic but true statement, that you need to repeat to yourself: &quot;Just because people are disagreeing with me and my idea, does not mean that I am more creative then everyone else here.&quot; Keep saying it until you believe it.<br /> <br /> Now, onto the meat of my reply. There are quite a few presumptions, and misstatements in your posts in this thread, so please tone down your anger that someone, on a public forum, might have the audacity to disagree with something that you posted. In which you mentioned that we were to &quot;Enjoy, discuss, or discard at your leisure&quot;. If you cannot, then this forum might not be a good place for you to frequent, and please, try not to take offense at we humble souls, we were just taking you at your word, and discussing and discarding your idea at our leisure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:10:12-07:00","id":1154686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154658#post1154658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this forum might not be a good place for you to frequent, and please, try not to take offense at we humble souls, we were just taking you at your word, and discussing and discarding your idea at our leisure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the unempathetic and frequently sarcastic responses I've recieved in this thread alone, I agree this forum is not for me. For those of you who were aspiring to troll me off the forum - congrads you've won. I've been abused enough before by guys online that I have no interest in making myself out to be a target for such mindless dismissal for what was originally a voluntary alternative.<br /> <br /> I'll be deleting my profile on here, walking away, and will look elsewhere for places to express my creativity. Thankyou for letting me know what this forum is before I became too invested in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:58:31-07:00","id":1154712,"title":"","content":"...Well, that just happened. <br /> <br /> Did I really come across as passive-aggressive? I wasn't trying to be or anything...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:20:14-07:00","id":1154717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154712#post1154712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Well, that just happened.<br /> <br /> Did I really come across as passive-aggressive? I wasn't trying to be or anything...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you were passive aggressive. You were critical, and with good reason. I can't for the life of me see any group implement this idea successfully and if it was to go anywhere it needed a serious examination. <br /> <br /> zenvious if you're still reading this forum, we're not trying to drive you away, we're pointing out flaws in your reasoning. We've done this to literally every person who's posted stuff to the forums. there used to be a guy who was one of the most frequent posters of user charms and we routinely tore them apart. He got better. So much better he's now one of the main guys designing the game. Hell, we still put the official stuff through the wringer. That's why there's an ask the Dev's thread for us to question and clarify and get errata right from the source.<br /> <br /> This forum is <i>amazing </i>for being able to thoughtfully examine and criticize ideas. But, damn, you've gotta be able to roll with the punches. Not all criticism is good or useful, but rejecting everything that disagrees with you is simply folly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:23:58-07:00","id":1154718,"title":"","content":"Seemed like yourself to me, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a>, and I've never known you to be passive aggressive before.<br /> <br /> But Occult being for Twilights isn't just about them being consummate sorcerers and craftsmen. It's also because Twilight is the time when the spooky things come out to haunt mankind. They don't show up when the sun is at its Zenith. The Priest-Kings would never see them during the light of day. It is to the Twilight to stand vigil against the oncoming darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:43:46-07:00","id":1154725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154371#post1154371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not the mystics</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, they technically are, if one is using the term in its real world connotation as an almost purely religious thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:54:25-07:00","id":1154727,"title":"","content":"Well, ok, but...<br /> <br /> Actually I figured out a better analogy to what I feel is wrong about the spread they suggested. Taking Occult from twilight and eclipse and giving it to zenith because of some notion that they should be more spiritually in-tune and do magic or whatever is a lot like if you took War from Dawn and Zenith and gave it to Twilight because its kind of a mental ability and twilights as problem solvers makes sense to cast as tacticians. <br /> <br /> Like, it makes sense on the surface but there's just a fundamental disconnect in the themes that makes it feel, y'know, wrong.<br /> <br /> I mean, that was the main thrust of my criticism. Not &quot;this is fine, don't change it&quot; but rather &quot;your reasoning displays a misunderstanding of what occult does and the crucial role it plays in the Twilight wheelhouse&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:15:22-07:00","id":1154736,"title":"","content":"I would still argue that Zenith's aren't &quot;mystics&quot; so much as &quot;priests.&quot; There are different connotations to the words that belie their individually similar meanings. &quot;Mystic&quot; has a more cerebral implication to it, whereas &quot;priest&quot; generally speaks to personal charisma rather than outright knowledge (though getting into a theological debate with a Jesuit or a Rabbi will likely end up with you having your intellectual ass handed to you, most people don't think of priests as being intellectuals for whatever reason). <br /> <br /> &quot;Mystics&quot; are &quot;mysterious.&quot; Zeniths are not mysterious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:17:36-07:00","id":1154737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154619#post1154619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P.S.: if you had been enjoying my work, it would have been appreciated if you had spoken up on it earlier to give me encouragement to keep trying to debate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read my post closer. I was on the way home on the bus when reading this topic. There was no way I could've responded until then (At least not in a way that didn't want me to punch my eyes out using my phone keyboard)<br /> <br /> That said I encourage all works, but reading over this made me had some questions before I could even start.<br /> <br /> 1) Are the rest of the abilities the same?<br /> 2) Do you still get the 5 favored abilities in addition to five caste?<br /> <br /> Either one of these are going to effect how I'd view the final product.<br /> <br /> You're also free to come and go as you please from these boards, but if you consider this level of criticism to be trolling then you ain't gonna get far with your work if you're truly passionate about it, just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:11:00-07:00","id":1154756,"title":"","content":"I just realised what ability might work better with Zenith. They're priests, right? Clerics. Healers. Give them <i>medicine.</i><br /> <br /> It even works with the currently presented system. Just swap medicine with occult in the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:51:24-07:00","id":1154770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154727#post1154727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, ok, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNote that I wasn't saying anything about them having Occult, just what the meaning of the term is and what it implies about the range of possibilities for characterizing Zeniths.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frish</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mystic&quot; has a more cerebral implication to it</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich might be why they have Lore as a Caste Ability now.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus, Integrity is one of their Caste Abilities, and that's where the game put the whole &quot;meditate yourself into a state of such serenity and attunement to the world that you become an immovable and indestructible calm centre of the universe&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frish</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeniths are not mysterious.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say that one not all there Wyld mutant hermit from the Caste Book could make a good run at it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough I think &quot;mysterious&quot;, at least as you seem to be implying it, is a bit of a narrow brush to paint every brand of mysticism with. I wouldn't exactly call Sufi Dervishes mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:27:35-07:00","id":1154781,"title":"","content":"All fair points, though I was merely pointing out how &quot;mystic&quot; and &quot;mysterious&quot; bear similar etymological heritages and, individual members notwithstanding, as a generalization one would not consider Zeniths to be &quot;mysterious.&quot; An individual Zenith can be mysterious. The Zenith Caste, as a whole, are not. <br /> <br /> And I was just thinking before checking here that if any Ability was integral to the core of a Zenith such that no one else gets it as a Caste Ability, it would be Integrity, partly for those Charms you mentioned but also because of the whole &quot;screw you, my faith is proof against your blandishments!&quot; aspect that, to me, is something that cannot be separated from the idea of a Zenith.<br /> <br /> Lore, though, also possesses all the teaching Charms, all the &quot;prophecy&quot; Charms...and that one capstone Charm that lets you call down a behemoth on an area that hast displeased you, Elijah-style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:49:06-07:00","id":1154789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154756#post1154756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realised what ability might work better with Zenith. They're priests, right? Clerics. Healers. Give them <i>medicine.</i><br /> <br /> It even works with the currently presented system. Just swap medicine with occult in the table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154718#post1154718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Occult being for Twilights isn't just about them being consummate sorcerers and craftsmen. It's also because Twilight is the time when the spooky things come out to haunt mankind. They don't show up when the sun is at its Zenith. The Priest-Kings would never see them during the light of day. It is to the Twilight to stand vigil against the oncoming darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>These two lines work for me; justifying why the Zenith shouldn't have Occult/ why the Twilight should. And also good justifiction for why the Zenith should have Medicine. Thankyou for these. They have helped.<br /> <br /> I will still remove myself from the forum for now. From my reaction, I'm clearly not ready to expose my ideas and suggestions to an online community just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:07:34-07:00","id":1154794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154789#post1154789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> These two lines work for me; justifying why the Zenith shouldn't have Occult/ why the Twilight should. And also good justifiction for why the Zenith should have Medicine. Thankyou for these. They have helped.<br /> <br /> I will still remove myself from the forum for now. From my reaction, I'm clearly not ready to expose my ideas and suggestions to an online community just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best way to become able to deal with criticism and learn the difference between well intentioned suggestions and sarcasm is to join a community. I'm an autistic person who was extensively bullied. I don't know what your experiences were, but if you've had bad experiences in the past, this is a good chance to overcome them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:29:35-07:00","id":1154799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154794#post1154794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way to become able to deal with criticism and learn the difference between well intentioned suggestions and sarcasm is to join a community. I'm an autistic person who was extensively bullied. I don't know what your experiences were, but if you've had bad experiences in the past, this is a good chance to overcome them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair call. My situation is similar. This was partially an effort to do as you've suggested. I have creativity and want to share it, but same time my ego has been smashed hard on multiple occasions that I've gone from wanting to help share and try to inspire others, to feeling that the internet is too brutal for someone as sensitive as I am these days to risk being hurt again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:48:21-07:00","id":1154810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154799#post1154799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair call. My situation is similar. This was partially an effort to do as you've suggested. I have creativity and want to share it, but same time my ego has been smashed hard on multiple occasions that I've gone from wanting to help share and try to inspire others, to feeling that the internet is too brutal for someone as sensitive as I am these days to risk being hurt again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the feeling. But the only way to become less sensitive is exposure, and reminding yourself that not everyone is your enemy, <i>and</i> that you have much to learn. That's the only way to improve. Don't think of it as people attacking your work. Think of it as you offering what you have to the forum, and in turn, they offer what <i>they</i> have to you. That way, you can benefit from everyone's experiences. In the end, if this is the homebrew you prefer, keep it for your use, but consider all the collective years of Exalted experience here. People who've had these debates and discussions and homebrew over and over, and have a lot of wisdom to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:33:41-07:00","id":1154826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1154067-my-alternate-solar-favored-abilities?p=1154781#post1154781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I was just thinking before checking here that if any Ability was integral to the core of a Zenith such that no one else gets it as a Caste Ability, it would be Integrity, partly for those Charms you mentioned but also because of the whole &quot;screw you, my faith is proof against your blandishments!&quot; aspect that, to me, is something that cannot be separated from the idea of a Zenith.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDo you mean it is, or it should be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:45:53-07:00","id":1154830,"title":"","content":"Couple cents, Zeniths got Lore and not Occult in 3e I think because kings need to be smart, not know how to talk to spirits, generally. It's notable that Zeniths can interact with spirits wihtout a dot of Occult because if all else fials, the Zenith can <i>make </i>spirits deal with the Zenith on her own terms by forcing them to manifest. Then you deal with them like you do with everything else: Talking with them or beating the ever living shit out of them.<br /> <br /> Lore is there to me to get you like, the philosopher-king from Plato's <i>Republic</i> or to be Markus Aurelius. Zeniths aren't dealing with the uncanny because they're not D&amp;D priests with detect evil and which channel spirits. They are indivdiuals who have overwelming ability to persuade, survive or know. I think it's notable that in the default list, the eight Abilities Zeniths have more or less are about 1) Overwelming force of personality (Performance, Presence), 2) Overwelming physical prowess (Athletics, Resistance, Survival), 3) Overcoming hardships (Integrity, Resistance, Survival) and 4) Knowing more about the physical world (Survival, Lore). They're to me the most &quot;Lead by being the best god-damned person at stuff&quot; possible Caste and so reflect htat.<br /> <br /> Compare with Twilights who are just really cerebral. The thing tha ties Occult, Lore, Linguistics, Medicine, and Bureaucracy is that they're all the persuits of the learned and the trained academic. They get Occult because it's an area of specialized, scholarly knowledge, and such. Along with again, things you generally just associate with learned scholars, doctors or academics. Exorcisms and the occult in Exalted draw on pretty specific themes. And a bit of that is this more I would say scholarly than theocratic bent. In many fantasy settings, the stuff Occult doe sis very much tied with priests (cliche Turn Undead and divine magic in D&amp;D). In Creation, Occult is the persuit of the weird, but it is still a persuit of scholarly folk. It's soemthing that results in